<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ergeme</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1560</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ergeme was fought on 2 August 1560 near Ērģeme in northern Latvia during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>. A Russian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> destroyed a force of the Livonian Order, capturing the land marshal Philipp Schall von Bell, who was later executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. It was the order's last battle in the field, and within two years the order was dissolved.</p></div>
